## Why this pin and not upstream HEAD

v1.92.8 is a tagged release, AND it is the exact commit the BioShock Trilogy VR
mod ships (`third_party/imgui` submodule SHA in that repo, verified against this
tag). That mod is one of the three read at source for REVIEW-VRMENU-2026-08, and
PLAN-VRMENU M1 adapts its 179-line overlay — so the code being adapted is known
to build and run against exactly these sources. Pinning to a version nothing has
exercised would throw that away for no gain.

## Why in-tree rather than FetchContent

PLAN-VRMENU §1.5. Deploys in this project are hash-verified, and a build input
that can change without a commit is precisely what a hash verification exists to
rule out. The OpenXR SDK uses FetchContent in plugin/CMakeLists.txt; that is a
pre-existing exception, not a precedent to widen.

## What is here, and what is deliberately not

Present: imgui.cpp, imgui_draw.cpp, imgui_tables.cpp, imgui_widgets.cpp,
imgui.h, imgui_internal.h, imconfig.h, the three imstb_*.h that imgui.cpp
includes, LICENSE.txt, and backends/imgui_impl_dx11.{h,cpp} and
backends/imgui_impl_win32.{h,cpp}.

ABSENT ON PURPOSE: imgui_demo.cpp. PLAN-VRMENU §1.5 excludes it from the shipped
build. It is ~2000 lines of widget gallery that would be linked into a DLL that
is injected into the wearer's game.

## Local modifications

NONE. If that ever stops being true, list every change here with its reason —
an unlisted local edit to a pinned dependency is indistinguishable from a
version mismatch when something breaks.
